[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5017128772","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121387#issuecomment-5017128772","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121387","id":5017128772,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKwtPRA","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-19T19:44:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-19T19:44:11Z","body":"Found a minor issue; if you start in landscape then rotate, part of the UI will be cut-off \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dceb309a-0e80-4899-a2cf-4582f40ae8e8\r\n\r\nI think when calculating the scale, we may want to use the smallest dimensions always regardless of orientation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5017128772/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5017162692","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121387#issuecomment-5017162692","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121387","id":5017162692,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKwvTxA","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-19T19:55:32Z","updated_at":"2026-07-19T19:55:32Z","body":"I did a quick test and I think we can enable portrait orientation for all workspaces except the game workspace when distraction free mode is enabled, using the same logic as for the script editor.\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e443b76f-8b3b-40bc-bd85-b305776601a8\r\n\r\nStill some minor issues that will need polish:\r\n- The 2D and 3D workspaces' menu bar goes beyond the width available in portrait, and are not scrollable.\r\n- The right virtual joysticks in the 3D workspace renders out of screen\r\n- The touch action panel now takes valuable space in portrait, wondering if we should move it to the bottom when in portrait.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5017162692/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5017303216","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121387#issuecomment-5017303216","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121387","id":5017303216,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKw34sA","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-19T20:41:50Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T20:40:50Z","body":"> Found a minor issue; if you start in landscape then rotate, part of the UI will be cut-off\r\n> \r\n>  screen-20260719-123934-1784489959664.mp4 \r\n> I think when calculating the scale, we may want to use the smallest dimensions always regardless of orientation.\r\n\r\nWe are already using the smallest one. In portrait, we just switch default window size because those are originally for landscape. So the calculated scale should be same in both landscape and portrait.\r\n\r\nEdit: I think I know what's happening, this issue can happen if `DisplayServer.screen_get_size()` returns different values, I mean the height returned in landscape doesn't match the width returned in portrait.\r\n\r\nEdit: I can reproduce the issue but not sure about the exact cause. It's doesn't seem related to scalling but instead godot UI logic.\r\nI found out that, this issue is only happening on certain editor scales, for instance if scale is 1.72 and you start in landscape it will cause the issue. But if scale is 1.75 (175%) (notice i actually increased the scale), it won't cause that issue. Similarly, it causes the issue even in 1.5(150%) scale","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5017303216/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5063201014","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121387#issuecomment-5063201014","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121387","id":5063201014,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLcpQ9g","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T20:40:08Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T18:22:21Z","body":"@KoBeWi any idea about https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121387#issuecomment-5017128772 ?\r\n\r\nI found out that, this issue is only happening on certain editor scales, for instance if scale is 1.72 and you start in landscape it will cause the issue. But if scale is 1.75 (175%) (notice i actually increased the scale), it won't cause that issue. ~Similarly, it causes the issue even in 1.5(150%) scale.~\r\n\r\nIt seems like Godot Control nodes are not resizing properly on certain scale.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5063201014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5069689109","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121387#issuecomment-5069689109","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121387","id":5069689109,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLi1RFQ","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://